\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces (a) Only the canonicalisation clears the noise floor; the two mechanisms built for the sixth degree of freedom sit inside it. (b) The non-equivariance residual of Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\eqref  {eq:resid} falls as training data grows, so the property an equivariant architecture would impose is emerging on its own; the hollow marker shows that removing roll augmentation raises the residual but leaves it small, so augmentation was not the cause of the near-equivariance}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanisms}{{2}{6}{(a) Only the canonicalisation clears the noise floor; the two mechanisms built for the sixth degree of freedom sit inside it. (b) The non-equivariance residual of Eq.~\eqref {eq:resid} falls as training data grows, so the property an equivariant architecture would impose is emerging on its own; the hollow marker shows that removing roll augmentation raises the residual but leaves it small, so augmentation was not the cause of the near-equivariance}{figure.2}{}}
